  "name": "budget flags: units and validation are inconsistent across commands",
  "slug": "budget-flags-units-and-validation",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "budget flags: units and validation are inconsistent across commands",
    "details_md": "show --context --budget N means N*4 chars while context --budget N means N chars; context rejects negatives (exit 2) but ready/status/search/events accept them and return everything-elided (agents may misread empty ready as nothing ready). Also show --context appends a ~33-char note after slicing so tiny budgets overshoot.",
    "acceptance": [
      "one documented unit everywhere",
      "negative budgets rejected consistently"
    ],
